{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791660174,"nonce":"Q5anOo35mjZHq7dgzVVM6aYFV0w=","title":"Containers: container path mode (JOBHUNTER_CONTAINER=1)","message":"Spec 018 section Container mode (ticket C1). Add an explicit container mode switched on by JOBHUNTER_CONTAINER=1 (set in the image, never auto-detected from /run/.containerenv because toolbox and distrobox have that file). In container mode: XDG defaults become config /config, data /data, cache /cache (explicit JOBHUNTER_* path vars and config.toml still win), jobhunter paths prints mode container and the source label container default, migrate-paths and schedule install/uninstall refuse with a pointer to the host, the legacy-data guard is skipped, .env files are read only from JOBHUNTER_ENV_FILE (not ./.env or ~/.env), mail auth without --manual refuses, keyring is not tried, and console may bind 0.0.0.0 without --allow-remote while the Host and Origin loopback check stays exactly as it is (allow_remote stays False). Checks the worker can do without podman: unit tests with monkeypatched env for every item above, including a test that cross_site_reason still refuses a non-loopback Host in container mode; ruff and pytest. Needs host or CI: only the C8 smoke test.","files":null}]}